1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:15,108
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today, November sixteenth: yesterday was a special day when families take their young children, dressed in kimonos, to shrines. Let's listen.

2
00:00:15,708 --> 00:00:21,371
[News] 11月15日は「七五三」の日でした。

3
00:00:22,071 --> 00:00:33,280
[News] 七五三は、3歳、5歳、7歳の子どもが、元気に大きくなったことをお祝いする日です。

4
00:00:33,979 --> 00:00:41,683
[News] この日、日本の各地の神社は、たくさんの家族でにぎわいました。

5
00:00:42,384 --> 00:00:49,584
[News] 子どもたちは、きれいな着物を着て、神社にお参りしました。

6
00:00:50,283 --> 00:00:57,915
[News] 家族は、子どもがこれからも元気に育つように、お願いしました。

7
00:00:58,615 --> 00:01:06,176
[News] 子どもたちは、「千歳あめ」という、細くて長いあめをもらいました。

8
00:01:06,876 --> 00:01:13,691
[News] 鹿児島市は晴れて、家族は笑顔で写真をとっていました。

9
00:01:14,391 --> 00:01:22,840
[News] 山形市は雨でしたが、神社には1日に約50の家族が来ました。

10
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:30,260
[News] 着物とぞうりで歩くのが、少し大変な子どももいました。

11
00:01:30,959 --> 00:01:39,599
[News] 将来の夢を聞くと、「ケーキを作る人になりたい」と答えた子どももいました。

12
00:01:40,299 --> 00:01:42,364
[Host] Now let's break it down.

13
00:01:42,963 --> 00:01:49,036
[Slow] 11月15日は「七五三」の日でした。

14
00:01:49,835 --> 00:01:54,084
[Host] November fifteenth was the day of the Seven-Five-Three festival.

15
00:01:54,683 --> 00:02:06,707
[Slow] 七五三は、3歳、5歳、7歳の子どもが、元気に大きくなったことをお祝いする日です。

16
00:02:07,507 --> 00:02:13,364
[Host] It's a day to celebrate three, five and seven-year-old children growing up healthy.

17
00:02:13,963 --> 00:02:16,219
[Vocab] お祝い

18
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:21,515
[Host] It means a celebration. With the verb for do, it means to celebrate.

19
00:02:22,116 --> 00:02:30,372
[Slow] この日、日本の各地の神社は、たくさんの家族でにぎわいました。

20
00:02:31,171 --> 00:02:35,972
[Host] On this day, shrines all over Japan were busy with families.

21
00:02:36,572 --> 00:02:38,972
[Vocab] にぎわう

22
00:02:39,372 --> 00:02:42,948
[Host] It means a place is lively and crowded with people.

23
00:02:43,548 --> 00:02:51,252
[Slow] 子どもたちは、きれいな着物を着て、神社にお参りしました。

24
00:02:52,051 --> 00:02:56,348
[Host] The children wore beautiful kimonos and visited the shrines.

25
00:02:56,948 --> 00:02:59,108
[Vocab] 着物

26
00:02:59,508 --> 00:03:03,348
[Host] It means a kimono, traditional Japanese clothing.

27
00:03:03,948 --> 00:03:06,252
[Vocab] お参り

28
00:03:06,651 --> 00:03:10,036
[Host] It means visiting a shrine or temple to pray.

29
00:03:10,635 --> 00:03:18,819
[Slow] 家族は、子どもがこれからも元気に育つように、お願いしました。

30
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:23,651
[Host] Families prayed that their children would keep growing up healthy.

31
00:03:24,252 --> 00:03:26,604
[Vocab] 育つ

32
00:03:27,003 --> 00:03:31,228
[Host] It means to grow up, for children, animals or plants.

33
00:03:31,828 --> 00:03:39,939
[Slow] 子どもたちは、「千歳あめ」という、細くて長いあめをもらいました。

34
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:48,515
[Host] The children got a thin, long candy called thousand-year candy. Its long shape is a wish for a long life.

35
00:03:49,116 --> 00:03:56,436
[Slow] 鹿児島市は晴れて、家族は笑顔で写真をとっていました。

36
00:03:57,235 --> 00:04:02,828
[Host] In one city in the south it was sunny, and families smiled as they took photos.

37
00:04:03,427 --> 00:04:05,587
[Vocab] 笑顔

38
00:04:05,987 --> 00:04:09,084
[Host] It means a smiling face, or a smile.

39
00:04:09,683 --> 00:04:18,732
[Slow] 山形市は雨でしたが、神社には1日に約50の家族が来ました。

40
00:04:19,531 --> 00:04:26,036
[Host] In a city in the north it rained, but about fifty families came to one shrine in a single day.

41
00:04:26,636 --> 00:04:33,836
[Slow] 着物とぞうりで歩くのが、少し大変な子どももいました。

42
00:04:34,636 --> 00:04:40,108
[Host] Some children found it a little hard to walk in a kimono and traditional sandals.

43
00:04:40,708 --> 00:04:42,939
[Vocab] 大変

44
00:04:43,339 --> 00:04:45,403
[Host] It means hard or tough.

45
00:04:46,004 --> 00:04:55,267
[Slow] 将来の夢を聞くと、「ケーキを作る人になりたい」と答えた子どももいました。

46
00:04:56,067 --> 00:05:01,468
[Host] Asked about their dreams, one child said, I want to be someone who makes cakes.

47
00:05:02,067 --> 00:05:04,348
[Vocab] 将来

48
00:05:04,747 --> 00:05:08,564
[Host] It means the future, especially a person's future.

49
